    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159-a2">

                <pb facs="0414" n="318" xml:id="pg318"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander Kautz to Mr. Henderson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Steamer Monocacy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Amoy, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 5,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 4th instant, requesting my co-operation in
                    compelling the Americans to leave the forces of the Japanese now in Formosa.</p>
                <p>I have referred the matter by telegraph to the commander-in-chief of the United
                    States naval forces on the Asiatic station, and will advise you of the nature of
                    his reply as soon as I receive it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. KAUTZ,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Commander United States
                            Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
